Consider two covariant functors $F: \mathscr A \to \mathscr B$ and $G: \mathscr B \to \mathscr A$ that form an adjoint pair $(F, G)$. For every $A \in \mathscr A$ and $B \in \mathscr B$, there exists a natural bijection:

$$\tau_{AB}: \operatorname{Mor}_{\mathscr B}(F(A), B) \to \operatorname{Mor}_{\mathscr A}(A, G(B)).$$

The naturality condition requires that for any morphism $g: B \to B'$ in $\mathscr B$, the following diagram commutes:

$$\require{AMScd}
\begin{CD}
\operatorname{Mor}_{\mathscr A}(A, G(B)) @>Gg^*>> \operatorname{Mor}_{\mathscr A}(A, G(B')) \\
@V\tau_{AB}^{-1}VV @V\tau_{AB'}^{-1}VV \\
\operatorname{Mor}_{\mathscr B}(F(A), B) @>g^*>> \operatorname{Mor}_{\mathscr B}(F(A), B')
\end{CD}$$

Does this diagram correctly illustrate the requirement for naturality when $g: B \to B'$?

Given the joint probability density function for random variables $X$ and $Y$:
\[ f(x, y)=\begin{cases}
2(x+y)  & \text{if } 0<x<y<1 \\
0 &  \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}. \]
Find the real number $a$ such that the conditional expectation $E(X | Y=aX)=\frac{2}{9}$. \(a\) is a real number.

Consider the quadratic function \( f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c \), where \( a, b, c \in \mathbf{R} \) and \( a \neq 0 \). The function satisfies the following conditions:
1. \( f(-1) = 0 \);
2. For all \( x \in \mathbf{R} \), \( f(x) \geq x \);
3. For \( x \in (0, 2) \), \( f(x) \leq \frac{(x+1)^2}{4} \).

Given \( x_1, x_2, x_3 \in (0, 2) \) such that \( \frac{1}{x_1} + \frac{1}{x_2} + \frac{1}{x_3} = 3 \), determine the minimum value of \( f(x_1) f(x_2) f(x_3) \).

Evaluate the sum \( \sum_{n=-\infty}^\infty f(n) \), where for any integer \( n \), \( k(n) = \frac{n^7}{7} + \frac{n^3}{3} + \frac{11n}{21} + 1 \) and
\[
f(n) = \begin{cases}
0 & \text{if } k(n) \text{ is an integer} \\
\frac{1}{n^2} & \text{if } k(n) \text{ is not an integer}
\end{cases}
\]

Given the joint density function of the two-dimensional variable \((X, Y)\):
\[
f(x,y) = \begin{cases} 
2x^2 & \text{if } -1 < x < 1 \text{ and } 0 < y < |x| \\
0 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
\]
Compute the conditional expected value \(E(X-Y \mid X+Y = -0.5)\).

