Suppose that the bivariate random variable \((X,Y)\) has the joint density function:
\[
f_{X,Y}(x,y)=\left\{
 \begin{array}{ll}
  1  & \mbox{when } y > 0 , x+y<1 \text{ and } y<x+1 \\
  0 & \mbox{otherwise }
 \end{array}
\right.
\]
Find \(\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)\).

